  "summary": "My biggest passion is finding solutions to problems that affect myself or others. I love learning and get excited about applying new technologies and tools. Edge cases and potential problems are the first thing that come to my mind when implementing a feature or change.\n\nWhen I began studying CS, I jumped straight into fullstack development for a realworld web application to streamline the bidding process for our family business. Before I introduced our current system, we had been keeping track of incoming requests manually which led to operational gaps, such as misplaced requests.\n\nTo address this problem, I developed a responsive website, a bid stack and a content management system for the job pipeline in order to centralize customer job progression. I've made use of a variety of public APIs to enhance the accessibility and availability of this product. Any problems affecting consumers or administration are addressed with a timely SLA. As I build applications, customer satisfaction, usability, and simplicity are my key tenents.",
